  "composer": "James R. Murray",
  "about": "Jolly Old Saint Nicholas is a Christmas song that began as a poem by Emily Huntington Miller. Her poem was published as Lilly's Secret in the magazine The Little Corporal in December 1865. The music is generally believed to be by James R. Murray. It was first printed in 1874, in a school music book called School Chimes.",
  "funFact": "The bandleader Ray Conniff recorded the song in 1962, for his album We Wish You a Merry Christmas.",
